    title: "call_construct: amend the axiom, fix the cross-axis starvation-gate test, allowlist the vocabulary, drop two off-axis values"  # aa9f
    status: todo_hard  # aa9f
    priority: 2  # aa9f
    parent:  # aa9f
    tags:  # aa9f
    - taint  # aa9f
    isbefore: []  # aa9f
    duplicate_of: []  # aa9f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # aa9f
    pr_ref:  # aa9f
    description: "FROM audit-findings 0019 (docs/audits/0019-call-construct-value-family.md),\nthe 2026-09-10 fundamental-concept audit of `Edge.meta[\"call_construct\"]`.\nFour remedies, one item because they share a file and a test.\n\n(1) AMEND THE AXIOM. axis_meta_keys.py:305 says the key names the\n\"Source-language call construct\". Two shipped values are constructs that are\nNOT calls: `constructor` (defended in the registry itself -- ruby emits `calls`\nwhere dart/csharp emit `instantiates` for the same source construct, INV-kahig)\nand `assignment` (WI-dosuh: `ws.onmessage = h`). Reword to \"Source-language\nconstruct that produced this call-family edge\". No value migration; the wording\nis what the field has always meant. It is load-bearing, not cosmetic: under the\nliteral current wording `assignment` is off-axis.\n\n(2) FIX A CROSS-AXIS MEMBERSHIP TEST -- THE SILENT BUG. verify_claims.py:3908:\n\n    construct = (edge.get(\"meta\") or {}).get(\"call_construct\")\n    if construct and construct in module_kinds[language].get(module, set()):\n\n`module_kinds` is built from catalog.primitives (3850-3857), so it holds\nIoPrimitive.kind values, whose vocabulary is exactly {\"function\", \"method\"}\n(io_boundary.py:633). A call_construct value is membership-tested against a\nDIFFERENT axis's value set, and only works because two tokens coincide.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: for the other ten values the first satisfaction route can never\nfire. Every elixir `pipe`, erlang `local`/`remote`, haskell\n`application`/`monadic_action`, ocaml `application`, rust `macro_body`,\ndart/csharp `constructor` and javascript `assignment` call falls through to the\nsecond route regardless of what the module declares. No error, no log line --\nthe method-starvation gate silently degrades for eight languages. The\nsurrounding comment reasons in {function, method} terms throughout, so the\ntwo-value assumption is explicit in the prose and untrue of the field.\n\nNOT YET MEASURED: whether fixing it moves any verdict. Measure before and after\non a multi-language cohort; it may be inert, and if so say so rather than\nclaiming a win.\n\n(3) TURN THE DENYLIST INTO AN ALLOWLIST. test_axis_meta_keys.py:411 pins\n_FOLDED_CALL_CONSTRUCTS -- four values previously ejected, with a positive\ncontrol proving the walk fires. That is the right guard for REGRESSION and\ncannot stop a value it has never seen. `assignment` shipped 2026-09-10 through\nevery gate in the repo with no review of whether it belongs on this axis; the\naudit that caught it ran only because a commit-count cadence fired. Replace with\na declared allowlist so a new value must be added deliberately. Keep the\ndenylist's positive-control pattern -- a guard that cannot be shown to fire is\nindistinguishable from one whose walk matches nothing.\n\n(4) MIGRATE THE TWO DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD VALUES.\n  - `macro` (erlang.py:562): the same edge already carries\n    evidence_type=\"macro_expansion\"; call_construct=macro restates the inference\n    pathway on a second axis -- the exact rationale recorded for ejecting\n    `interface_dispatch`. tree-sitter expanded nothing at that site, so there is\n    no observed source call construct to name. Remove; the fact has a home.\n  - `macro_body` (rust.py:3123): names WHERE the call was found (inside a macro\n    token tree), not what it is. No uniform fold target --\n    _extract_macro_call_names yields Self::-qualified, ::-qualified and bare\n    callees, so the true construct varies per site. Either stamp the real\n    construct per site or stamp nothing.\nZERO consumers read either value (all 15 comparison sites test == \"method\"), so\nthis migration is producer-only and cannot change a verdict.\n\nORDERING NOTE: (3) should land AFTER (4), or the allowlist has to carry two\nvalues it is about to lose."  # aa9f
    fields: {}  # aa9f
- op: discuss  # 4157
  at: '2026-10-01T00:56:52Z'  # 4157
  by: agent  # 4157
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4157
  clock: 2  # 4157
  nonce: '4157'  # 4157
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. Remedies (1), (3), (4) hold as written. Remedy (2)'s code fact holds, but its stated CONSEQUENCE is overstated (details below). Read-only check: no tests run, no verdict A/B.\n\nDrift in the citations:\n- The audit is docs/surveys/call-construct-value-family-audit.md (3858e02445). docs/audits/0019 is a different audit (backend-agreement-rust-aardvark-dns).\n- Axiom wording: axis_meta_keys.py:334-348 still reads \"Source-language call construct collapsed under ast_call apex\". It now also defends 'constructor' in prose (INV-kahig), but the amendment proposed in (1) has not been made.\n- Membership test: verify_claims.py:4371-4372, in method_starved_modules (def at 4248); module_kinds is built at 4308-4320. The test is unchanged since INV-soval (46ca2dc353).\n- IoPrimitive.kind is now the io-primitive-kind axis {function, method, attribute} (io_primitive_kinds.py, ADR-0059), not io_boundary.py:633. 'attribute' is not a call_construct value, so the overlap is still two coinciding tokens.\n- Emit sites: erlang.py:599 'macro' (still carries evidence_type=macro_expansion); rust.py:3212 'macro_body'; the denylist is still at test_axis_meta_keys.py:411 with the same 4 values, and there is no allowlist.\n- A value the item does not list: 'protocol', emitted at py.py:5944 (dd3b7cf0ee, 2026-09-06) and covered by the survey audit at its line 63. Emitted values found by grep: 12, of which 10 are off-axis.\n\nCorrection to (2)'s consequence. method_starved_modules does `if not modules: continue` (verify_claims.py:4352) for any language that has no method-kind catalogue module. Measured with load_catalog(): elixir, erlang, haskell, ocaml, dart, csharp and ruby have 0 method-kind modules each. So for pipe, local, remote, application, monadic_action and dart/csharp 'constructor', the first route is never reached at all. There is no degradation there. Only these off-axis values reach the test:\n- python 'protocol', into django.db.models, which is a method-kind module through the community overlay;\n- js/ts 'assignment', whose dst is normally a local handler;\n- rust 'macro_body', whose dst is an in-repo target.\nWhether fixing (2) moves any verdict was NOT measured; the above makes \"inert\" the likely outcome to pre-register. The ZERO-consumers claim for macro/macro_body re-checked: no comparison against either value in packages/*/src.\n\nProposed item change: fix the audit path, and restate (2)'s consequence as \"reachable for python protocol / js assignment / rust macro_body only\"."  # 4157
