    description: "FROM the call_construct value-family fundamental-concept audit of 2026-09-10\n(docs/surveys/call-construct-value-family-audit.md), which audits\n`Edge.meta[\"call_construct\"]`. Four remedies, in one item because they share a\nfile and a test.\n\nVALUES EMITTED TODAY (grep of packages/*/src): method, function, pipe, local,\nremote, application, monadic_action, macro, macro_body, constructor,\nassignment, protocol. Ten of the twelve are neither `function` nor `method`.\n\n(1) AMEND THE AXIOM. axis_meta_keys.py:334-348 says the key names the\n\"Source-language call construct\". Two shipped values are constructs that are\nNOT calls:\n  - `constructor`, which the registry prose itself defends: ruby emits `calls`\n    where dart/csharp emit `instantiates` for the same source construct\n    (INV-kahig);\n  - `assignment` (WI-dosuh: `ws.onmessage = h`).\nReword to \"Source-language construct that produced this call-family edge\". No\nvalue migration: the new wording is what the field has always meant. This is\nload-bearing, not cosmetic, because under the literal current wording\n`assignment` is off-axis.\n\n(2) FIX A CROSS-AXIS MEMBERSHIP TEST. In method_starved_modules\n(verify_claims.py:4248), at lines 4371-4372:\n\n    construct = (edge.get(\"meta\") or {}).get(\"call_construct\")\n    if construct and construct in module_kinds[language].get(module, set()):\n\n`module_kinds` (built at 4308-4320 from catalog.primitives) holds IoPrimitive.kind\nvalues. Those belong to the io-primitive-kind axis {function, method, attribute}\n(io_primitive_kinds.py, ADR-0059). So a call_construct value is\nmembership-tested against a DIFFERENT axis's value set, and the test works only\nbecause two tokens coincide.\n\nCONSEQUENCE, SCOPED. The function skips any language with no method-kind\ncatalogue module (`if not modules: continue`, line 4352). elixir, erlang,\nhaskell, ocaml, dart, csharp and ruby have none, so pipe, local, remote,\napplication, monadic_action and dart/csharp `constructor` never reach this\ntest. The off-axis values that DO reach it, and always fall through to the\nsecond (name) route whatever the module declares, are:\n  - python `protocol` (py.py:5944), into django.db.models, a method-kind module\n    through the community overlay;\n  - js/ts `assignment`, whose dst is normally a local handler;\n  - rust `macro_body`, whose dst is an in-repo target.\nNo error, no log line.\n\nNOT YET MEASURED: whether fixing it moves any verdict. The scope above makes\n\"inert\" the likely outcome; pre-register that, measure before and after on a\npython + js + rust cohort, and if it is inert say so rather than claiming a\nwin.\n\n(3) TURN THE DENYLIST INTO AN ALLOWLIST. test_axis_meta_keys.py:411 pins\n_FOLDED_CALL_CONSTRUCTS: four values previously ejected, with a positive\ncontrol proving the walk fires. That is the right guard for REGRESSION, but it\ncannot stop a value it has never seen. `assignment` shipped 2026-09-10 through\nevery gate in the repo with no review of whether it belongs on this axis.\nReplace the denylist with a declared allowlist, so that a new value must be\nadded deliberately. Keep the positive-control pattern.\n\n(4) MIGRATE THE TWO DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD VALUES.\n  - `macro` (erlang.py:599): the same edge already carries\n    evidence_type=\"macro_expansion\", so call_construct=macro restates the\n    inference pathway on a second axis. That is the exact rationale recorded\n    for ejecting `interface_dispatch`. Remove it; the fact already has a home.\n  - `macro_body` (rust.py:3212): names WHERE the call was found (inside a macro\n    token tree), not what it is. There is no uniform fold target, because\n    _extract_macro_call_names yields Self::-qualified, ::-qualified and bare\n    callees. Either stamp the real construct per site or stamp nothing.\nZERO consumers compare against either value, so this migration is\nproducer-only.\n\nORDERING NOTE: (3) should land AFTER (4), or the allowlist has to carry two\nvalues it is about to lose.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # cd70
